message.content:
This is a women's panty (brief) of knit nylon/elastane fabric. Knit women's briefs and panties fall under HTSUS 6108.21 (cotton), 6108.22 (man-made fibers), or 6108.29 (other textile materials). Nylon and elastane are both man-made fibers, so 6108.22 applies. The statistical suffix for women's briefs and panties of man-made fibers is 6108.22.9020. The 6108.22.90 subheading covers items other than those containing 5 percent or more by weight of elastomeric yarn, and 6108.22.9020 is the "Women's" line.

The code 6108.22.9020 reads "Briefs and panties: Of man-made fibers: Other: Women's." I am not sure of this exact suffix, but I'm fairly confident the 6108.22.00 subheading breaks into 6108.22.30 and 6108.22.90, with .9020 as the women's line.

{"hts_code": "6108.22.9020", "reason": "Women's knit panties of predominantly nylon/elastane (man-made fibers) with a cotton gusset liner are classified as knit women's briefs and panties of man-made fibers in heading 6108."}
